            <ArticleTitle>Severe allergic contact dermatitis secondary to nitroglycerin in a transdermal therapeutic system.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>365-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe two cases with a rare adverse effect of severe allergic contact dermatitis secondary to usage of a disc containing nitroglycerin. The causal agent is most probably trinitroglycerin as was demonstrated by skin patch testing using the North American Contact Dermatitis Group Method.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
